@startuml
title P2 Explicit Targets, Inbox, and Transport Parity - Components

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

actor "Pulsar UI" as ui
actor "Telegram Adapter" as tg
actor "Support/Admin" as admin

package "Coordinator" {
  component "Common Media Ingest\nSubmitMedia / Upload / Normalize" as ingest
  component "Transmission Application Service\nCreate / Replay / Delete / Cancel" as txsvc
  component "Opaque Target Reference Service\nList / issue / bind / expire" as targetrefs
  component "Audience Resolver\nAir / Own / Explicit -> exact snapshot" as resolver
  component "Mixed-version Capability Policy\nClip + future track requirements" as capabilities
  component "Inbox and Receipt Query Service\nHistory / Pagination / Aggregates" as inboxsvc
  component "Rights and Policy Service\nVersion/hash display / accept / revoke\nper-upload rights reminder / report / disable" as rights
  component "Media ACL Authorizer\nGET /media + revoke fetch" as acl
  component "Delivery Runtime\nClip scheduler + track queue policy" as runtime
}

database "Store\nmedia_items\ntransmissions\ntransmission_targets\ntarget reference digests\nreports\nairs / air_members" as db
database "Inbox Projection\ntransmission_inbox_items\ntransmission_replay_lineage\ninbox + receipt cursor digests" as inboxdb
component "Air Membership and Presence\n(active Air, capabilities, DND)" as air
component "Windows/macOS Pulsars" as nodes

ui --> ingest : upload / record / select media
ui --> targetrefs : list authorized opaque trf_ capabilities
ui --> txsvc : create transmission\nreplay / delete / cancel
ui --> inboxsvc : GET history / inbox / receipts\nexplicit dismiss / replay only
ui --> rights : accept policy / report / mute

tg --> ingest : voice / audio / document
tg --> txsvc : identical delivery actions\nqueue / replace / targets
tg --> inboxsvc : status / receipts
tg --> rights : policy / report errors

tg --> targetrefs : issue references through\nverified Telegram ActorContext
targetrefs --> db : store only digest +\ncredential/domain/binding scope
targetrefs --> air : authorize current domain\nand binding generation
txsvc --> resolver : resolve + deduplicate\nthen apply include-origin
resolver --> air : current Air members\ncapabilities / DND
resolver --> targetrefs : resolve opaque selector\n404 for forged/stale/cross-scope
txsvc --> capabilities : fail whole create with\n422 unsupported_targets
txsvc --> runtime : schedule clip or main-program action
txsvc --> db : persist transmission\nsnapshot / expiry
inboxsvc --> inboxdb : exact-binding keyset reads\nopaque bounded cursor state\nidempotent dismiss / replay lineage
runtime --> db : update exact target receipt
runtime --> inboxdb : same transaction creates\none eligible target item
runtime --> nodes : prepare / play / queue / replace
acl --> db : authorize by target snapshot\nand disable / delete state
nodes --> acl : authenticated media fetch
rights --> db : versioned grants + audit\nreports / delete / disable
rights --> inboxdb : project canonical\nrevocation state
rights --> acl : revoke future fetch
admin --> rights : review report / disable actor

note right of inboxdb
Ownership is the immutable transmission target tuple,
including actor, slot and binding generation. There is
no Air-membership edge. Replacement bindings and later
members cannot inherit historical media or inbox rows.
Eligible terminal receipts are exactly-once by a unique
target tuple; replay lineage never rewrites the receipt.
HTTP returns ib_/hi_/ir_ capabilities and safe labels;
raw media, transmission, actor, orbit, slot, and binding
identifiers never cross the inbox/receipt read boundary.
end note

note bottom of txsvc
Application and production Telegram paths now enter
one common service. N-recipient personal delivery is
never rewritten as broadcast. Rollback-era direct rows
refuse an unrepresentable multi-target personal action.
end note

@enduml
